.TH WELL\-RETENTION 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 86590d34" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
well\-retention \- Delete or archive Well rows past their retention class; \-dry\-run only counts.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B well\-retention
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete or archive Well rows past their retention class; \-dry\-run only counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-batch \fIN\fR
rows per delete transaction (1..100000) (default 1000)
.TP
.B \-\-class \fISTRING\fR
run this class only
.TP
.B \-\-classes \fISTRING\fR
retention classes (compliance/retention/classes.yaml) (default /etc/unheaded/well/retention\-classes.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
count what each class would do; delete nothing
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-dir \fISTRING\fR
write well_retention.prom here (node_exporter textfile); empty: none
.TP
.B \-\-statement\-timeout \fIDURATION\fR
limit per statement (default 5m0s)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
